    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The build is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`), and the audit output confirms the new behaviour end-to-end:\n\n```\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSWV22716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n## What I changed and why\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** \u2014 new single-responsibility class `OwnerIdentityVersion` (model) owns the `\"V2\"` tag and the two ways it's mixed in, so the literal and the mixing rules live in exactly one place:\n- `identityRegion(region)` \u2192 `region + \"V2\"` (e.g. `NSW` \u2192 `NSWV2`), the region code used *inside* the identifiers.\n- `taggedInput(hashInput)` \u2192 appends `\"|V2\"` to a hash core.\n\nEach identifier now consumes it, so every value changes and can't collide with a v1 value:\n- `MemberIdGenerator` leads the member id with the tagged region (`NSWV2261A2B3C4D7`).\n- `HouseholdIdGenerator` hashes `normalize(lastName)|postcode|V2`.\n- `Owner.getIdentityKey()` hashes `\u2026|soundex(lastName)|V2`.\n\n**Kept plain (not identifiers)** \u2014 `getLocality()` still returns `NSW`, `getTimezone()` and `OwnerSegment` still derive from the plain locality. The tag only appears inside identifiers. I updated the now-stale Javadoc/OpenAPI text that claimed locality \"leads the memberId\".\n\n**Response shape** \u2014 in `openapi.yml`: added a top-level integer `apiVersion` and a nested `Identity` schema (holding `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId`), and removed those three from the top level. `OwnerMapper` sets `apiVersion` via `constant = \"2\"` and maps `identity` from the whole owner through a new `toIdentityDto` sub-mapping.\n\n**Audit schema v2** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent` gained `schemaVersion = 2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the (now v2) owner, keeping the audit concern in the audit record.\n\nRequest fields (`OwnerFields`) are untouched. No production code referenced the moved DTO fields.",
