    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, execution-ordered list of every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via **POST /api/owners**.\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. The caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, else 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (`@Valid @RequestBody`) \u2014 failures \u2192 400:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(...{0,2}\\.?$)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(1..10)`\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 each `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (LocalDate)\n   - (`postcode` has no annotation \u2014 validated later in code; `sharesHousehold` ignored)\n\n## Inside the controller method (`addOwner`), in order\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if the optional `Idempotency-Key` header matches a previously-created, still-existing owner, return that owner with 200 (no creation). *(side-effect: read)*\n4. **Address normalization** \u2014 trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST/RD/AVE; composes `address` from `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` when present. *(mutation)*\n5. **Custom required-fields validation** (`OwnerFieldsValidator`) \u2014 rejects blank/whitespace `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and requires at least one of `addressLine1`/`address` \u2192 400.\n6. **Postcode validation** (`PostcodeValidator`) \u2014 if present, must be 4 digits within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 400.\n7. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (MapStruct; ignores `id`, `pets`).\n8. **Telephone normalization** \u2014 to E.164, default country +61, with length/per-country checks \u2192 400. *(mutation)*\n9. **Email normalization** \u2014 null if blank; else regex-validate \u2192 lower-case \u2192 **disposable-domain check** \u2192 400. *(mutation)*\n10. **Future registration-date guard** \u2014 supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 400.\n11. **Business-day adjustment** \u2014 rolls Sat/Sun/2026 holidays forward, sets `registrationDate`. *(mutation)*\n12. **Daily-limit check** \u2014 `countOwnersRegisteredOn(date)`; \u2265100 \u2192 429. Sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. *(read + mutation)*\n13. **City-capacity check** \u2014 `countOwnersInCity(city)`; \u226550 \u2192 409. Sets `capacityWarning = count >= 40`. *(read + mutation)*\n14. **Household id** \u2014 if postcode present, SHA-256 over normalized `lastName` + `postcode`. *(mutation)*\n15. **Hard duplicate check** \u2014 `findOwnersByIdentityKey`; any non-deleted match \u2192 409. *(read)*\n16. **Soft-match flag** \u2014 same postcode + soundex(lastName) but different identity key sets `possibleDuplicateOf`. *(read + mutation)*\n\n## Persistence (`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`, `@Transactional`)\n\n17. For a new owner, computes/sets defaults: unique **`memberId`** (via `deduplicateMemberId`, appends `-2`, `-3`\u2026), **`namesakeCount`**, **`householdSize`**, **`membershipLevelCap`**. *(reads + mutations)*\n18. **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** \u2014 the only DB write. At flush, entity-level Bean Validation applies: `address` `@NotEmpty`, `city` `@NotEmpty`, `telephone` `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`; `deleted` defaults to `false`. (No `@PrePersist` callbacks; no unique DB constraints \u2014 uniqueness is enforced in code only.)\n\n## Post-save side-effects (in order)\n\n19. **Remember idempotency key** \u2014 in-memory map mutation.\n20. **Audit log** \u2014 writes to `AUDIT` logger: a human line plus a serialized `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON with a monotonic sequence.\n21. **Welcome notification** \u2014 writes one line to the `NOTIFY` logger with ownerId + memberId.\n22. **HTTP 201** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, body mapped to `OwnerDto`.\n\n## Two clarifications worth flagging\n\n- The \"event\" and \"welcome\" are **log lines only** \u2014 there is **no Spring `ApplicationEvent`, no email sending, and no password hashing** anywhere in this flow.\n- The controller method itself is **not** `@Transactional`; transactionality comes only from the service's `saveOwner`. So the pre-save read checks (steps 12\u201316) run outside that transaction, and the post-save log side-effects (steps 20\u201321) also run outside it."
